{"name":"Pawn Broker","hex":"#473430","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being held as security for a loan, or as a pledge.","An instance of pawning something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pledge; to stake or wager.","To give as security on a loan of money; especially, to deposit (something) at a pawn shop."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pawn"},{"term":"broker","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["comparative form of broke: more broke"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mediator between a buyer and seller.","A stockbroker."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/broker"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pawnbroker","blocks":[{"text":"A pawnbroker is an individual who offers secured loans to people by taking items of personal property as collateral. A pawnbrokering entity is called a pawnshop or  pawnbrokerage. While many items can be pawned, pawnshops typically accept jewelry, musical instruments, coins, gold, silver and firearms. Home-audio equipment, computers, video-game systems, televisions, cameras, and power tools became pawnable as the world entered the Information Age. The items pawned to the broker or shop are themselves called pledges, pawns, or simply the collateral."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Leihhaus_20140220.jpg/330px-Leihhaus_20140220.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pawnbroker","wikidata":"Q176637"},{"title":"Broker","blocks":[{"text":"A broker is a person or entity that arranges transactions between a buyer and a seller. This may be done for a commission when the deal is executed. A broker who also acts as a seller or as a buyer becomes a principal party to the deal. Neither role should be confused with that of an agent—one who acts on behalf of a principal party in a deal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Stockexchange.jpg/330px-Stockexchange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Broker","wikidata":"Q160117"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Helsingin_Pantti_Salomonkatu_3_Helsinki_20231117.jpg/500px-Helsingin_Pantti_Salomonkatu_3_Helsinki_20231117.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Helsingin_Pantti_Salomonkatu_3_Helsinki_20231117.jpg/1280px-Helsingin_Pantti_Salomonkatu_3_Helsinki_20231117.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Helsingin_Pantti_Salomonkatu_3_Helsinki_20231117.jpg/500px-Helsingin_Pantti_Salomonkatu_3_Helsinki_20231117.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Helsingin Pantti's pawnbroker in Helsinki, Finland in 2023","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHelsingin_Pantti_Salomonkatu_3_Helsinki_20231117.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Pawnbroker%27s_sign%2C_Camden_High_Street%2C_London.JPG/500px-Pawnbroker%27s_sign%2C_Camden_High_Street%2C_London.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Pawnbroker%27s_sign%2C_Camden_High_Street%2C_London.JPG/1280px-Pawnbroker%27s_sign%2C_Camden_High_Street%2C_London.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Pawnbroker%27s_sign%2C_Camden_High_Street%2C_London.JPG/500px-Pawnbroker%27s_sign%2C_Camden_High_Street%2C_London.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A London shop displays the traditional pawnbroker's sign","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w